/-!
# A261046

Irregular triangle read by rows: the first column consists of the odd numbers repeated but without the first 1. Row n (n>=0) contains floor(n/2)=1 terms. Every row contains successive odd numbers.

The 64 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `0`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A261046

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `0`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [1, 3, 3, 5, 5, 7, 5, 7, 9, 7,
    9, 11, 7, 9, 11, 13, 9, 11, 13, 15,
    9, 11, 13, 15, 17, 11, 13, 15, 17, 19,
    11, 13, 15, 17, 19, 21, 13, 15, 17, 19,
    21, 23, 13, 15, 17, 19, 21, 23, 25, 15,
    17, 19, 21, 23, 25, 27, 13, 15, 17, 19,
    21, 23, 25, 27]

/-- `flat` agrees with `flatData` on the known range. -/
@[simp]
theorem flat_data_eq (n : flatArgType) (h : n < 64) : flat n = flatData[n]! := sorry

